sections.body_md:
Under the 2019 Act a complaint can be filed by:
- a **consumer**;
- a **voluntary consumer association** registered under any law;
- the **Central Government**, the Central Consumer Protection Authority or a **State Government**;
- **one or more consumers** on behalf of numerous consumers having the same interest;
- the **legal heir or legal representative** of a consumer who has died (and the parent or guardian of a minor consumer).

Complaints can be filed in person or **online**, and the complainant may argue the case without a lawyer.
